HandOverTheAccountTest
├── when anyone executes the handover after the wait
│   └── it should install the new key, remove the lost one, release the approval once and pay the order
├── when a call in the batch reverts
│   ├── it should revert
│   └── it should leave the attempt waiting and executable once the cause is gone
├── when the same batch is sent again
│   ├── it should revert
│   └── it should spend nothing a second time
├── when the payee reenters with the same batch
│   └── it should refuse the nested run and complete the outer one once
├── when the payment pays nobody
│   └── it should complete the handover with the payee unpaid
├── when a batch carries an extra call
│   └── it should revert
├── when the handover removes the kit slot
│   └── it should revert
├── when the handover installs the zero address
│   └── it should revert
├── when the handover names one address on both sides
│   └── it should revert
├── when the new key gained a privilege during the wait
│   └── it should revert
├── when the order has no amount
│   └── it should run the three calls and pay nothing
├── when the named native payee reverts
│   └── it should revert
└── when the new key sends the spend again
    └── it should revert
